=== 3. DECISIONS AND WHY ===
- cfront: dead end. OpenTTD needs C++20 (required since 14.0); cfront is ~C++2.x/3.0
  (no full templates/STL/lambdas).
- No maintained modern C++-to-C *source* translator exists (as far as found).
- C++-to-Go: not realistic for this code base; also Go's Plan 9 port is "experimental" and
  whether Go draw libs work on native Plan 9 (vs p9p's devdraw) was NOT verified.
- CHOSEN pipeline: clang -> LLVM IR -> llvm-cbe -> C -> Plan 9 C compiler.
    OpenTTD tag -> clang++ (C++20, -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti, fixed triple)
      -> per-TU IR (+ libc++ built to IR) -> llvm-link + internalize/globaldce
      -> llvm-cbe (patched) -> lowering to Plan 9 C dialect -> 6c/6l (mk on Plan 9)
- Plan B (not tried): clang -> freestanding x86-64 objects -> lld at Plan 9 load addresses
  -> a.out wrapper + syscall/ABI shim. More robust, but not a translator.
- Exceptions are disabled (-fno-exceptions makes try/catch a hard clang error, which is
  deliberate: cbe's LowerInvokePass would otherwise silently drop handlers).

